WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.090
Across period 3, each element has
one more proton than the one before.

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:11.250
So you'd expect each element's outer electron to
be harder to remove than the previous element's.

3
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.050
Magnesium needs 738 kilojoules per mole.

4
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.650
But aluminium, next along, needs only 578.

5
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.690
If nuclear charge rises across the period,

6
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.050
why does aluminium lose an electron
more easily than magnesium?

7
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:32.490
In this mission, you'll find two dips
in ionization energy across period 3,

8
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.730
and see what they reveal about
the energy levels inside atoms.

9
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:41.030
You'll explain each dip by comparing
the electrons that are removed.

10
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:46.600
Your mission: explain why aluminium loses
an electron more easily than magnesium.
